# Useful Helpers sidecar - installed copy.
#
# This is the PAYLOAD's ignore file, substituted at export time. The development
# repository's .gitignore names the parts bin, the harness, gates and trash - zones
# that do not exist in an installed sidecar, and whose names would tell a target
# about the sidecar's build process. Shipping it would leak build-time shape into
# a delivered artifact.
#
# An installed sidecar keeps its own memory. If the operator version-controls it,
# these are the things that must not be committed.

# Durable memory: the journal, evidence, the event log, the workbench map.
# This is the TARGET's history and belongs to whoever the sidecar is attached to.
_state/

# Disposable, regenerable exhaust.
_artifacts/
_exports/
logs/

# Derived from tools/*/tool.json; regenerated on demand.
config/registry.json

# Python bytecode and environments.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Databases and logs produced while working.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.log
